<!--
    Live value of cattle against standard genes (PRICE-BREED-03, RLBreedingValue). Live trade only:
    what the dealer pays and asks, the herdsman's trades and the payments that are a share of an
    animal's live value. Carcass yield, slaughter, contracts and meat prices do not read it.

    Standard (every gene 1) is the base: the animal's curve price (Animal:getCurvePrice, the HARD
    calibration) without the old fixed state parts, plus alphaNormal x the value of its present
    state against an open, dry animal of its age (a calf on the way, the rest of this lactation).
    Genes then move the price asymmetrically, from a reference cash flow over the animal's
    remaining breeding life in game money (milk at the best station's annual mean price, calves at
    the newborn curve price, offspring meat at the annual mean meat price):

        own     = PV(own genes)   - PV(standard genes)            milk, calvings, staying in the herd
        hered   = PV(+offspring)  - PV(own genes)                 future calves' inherited genes
        female  = standard - alphaNormal x losses + alphaOwn x rhoOwn x own+
                           + alphaHered x rhoHered x E(q) x hered+
        sire    = curve price + alphaHered x rhoHered x E(q) x (own + hered)+   (no loss: a poor
                  bull is a meat bull)
        E(q)    = 0 up to excellenceThreshold, convex to 1 at excellenceTop (excellenceK), q the
                  breed's weighted genetic score (dairy / beef terminal for bulls / beef maternal
                  for cows, mixed by dairyShare)

    A cow's meat gene is priced once, by what it adds to her slaughter value; a bull's stays in his
    curve price (a meat animal). The price stays between the meat route (slaughter value; a bull's
    curve price; a calf too young for the butcher the lower of her curve and her breed's bull
    curve: fattening) and the standard plus the whole PV gain.
    Castrated and infertile (fertility 0) animals are priced on the meat route only.

    Every value here is a game-economy candidate, not fitted to market data. Each is looked up by
    subType name, then breed within the animal type, then animal type, then this root element.
    To change them without editing the mod, copy this file to
    modSettings/FS25_RealisticLivestockRM/breedingValue.xml (it then replaces this file).

    enabled              1 prices cattle so, 0 keeps the old curve price with the fixed bonuses.
    alphaNormal          Share of standard production value paid, and of a shortfall taken off.
    alphaOwn, rhoOwn     Share of the animal's own gain paid, and confidence in it.
    alphaHered, rhoHered Share of the offspring gain paid, and confidence in it.
    discountRate         Yearly discount of the cash flow.
    annualExitRisk       Yearly chance a cow or bull leaves the herd at health gene 1;
                         x exp(-healthExitSlope x (health - 1) / 0.75).
    referenceOpenMonths  Months open after the wait at fertility 1. Other fertility scales it by
                         the game's conception odds ((1 - f/2) / (f/2)), between minOpenMonths
                         and maxOpenMonths.
    postpartumWaitMonth  Months after calving before she can conceive (the game: 3).
    femaleBirthSlots     Most future calvings counted.  breedingExitAgeMonth  No calving after.
    dairyShare           Share of milk sold (1 dairy, 0 beef); also mixes the score weights.
    milkNetShare         Share of the milk price a standard cow's milk nets after all its costs.
    milkIncrementShare   Share of the milk price extra milk (productivity) nets after its feed.
    offspringCapture     Share of an offspring's gain its parent's buyer can count on.
    sonSlaughterAgeMonth When a son's meat is sold.
    sireFemalesPerSeason, sireSeasons, sireConception, sireExitAgeMonth  A bull's own herd: cows
                         served a season, seasons counted, calves per cow served, last age.
    sireCapture          Share of a bull's offspring gain his buyer counts on (bought semen of the
                         same merit competes with him).
    sireQualificationAtBirth  Chance a bull calf proves out as a sire, rising to 1 at breeding age.
    w*                   Score weights (dairy, beef terminal sire, beef maternal cow).
-->
<breedingValue enabled="1"
               alphaNormal="0.60" alphaOwn="0.35" alphaHered="0.65" rhoOwn="0.85" rhoHered="0.85"
               excellenceThreshold="1.10" excellenceTop="1.75" excellenceK="5"
               discountRate="0.10" annualExitRisk="0.14" healthExitSlope="0.35"
               referenceOpenMonths="1.5" minOpenMonths="0.5" maxOpenMonths="8" postpartumWaitMonth="3"
               femaleBirthSlots="4" breedingExitAgeMonth="96" dairyShare="0.5"
               milkNetShare="0.25" milkIncrementShare="0.40"
               offspringCapture="0.60" sonSlaughterAgeMonth="20"
               sireFemalesPerSeason="24" sireSeasons="3" sireConception="0.90" sireExitAgeMonth="132"
               sireCapture="0.50" sireQualificationAtBirth="0.50"
               wDairyProductivity="0.40" wDairyFertility="0.30" wDairyHealth="0.30"
               wTerminalQuality="0.70" wTerminalFertility="0.20" wTerminalHealth="0.10"
               wMaternalQuality="0.45" wMaternalFertility="0.35" wMaternalHealth="0.20">
